 Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:17:34-07:00","id":1464186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464179#post1464179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ventrue one is alright but the rest are the bad the brujah look like eurotrash visiting a gay club they're not welcome at.<br /> The nosfertu one looked this fashion show trash chique. They wernt even ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather put the Ventrue as less stupid, but they sure are the best ones. All the other just shout &quot;Fashion Week&quot; to me, highly abstract and conceptual, no actual usefulness. They're not necessarily bad, although many are, but completely miss the point ad make the book all the worse just by being there.<br /> <br /> To me the Gangrel and Malkavian try hard to be the more offensive, with the Gangrel being extra ugly and nonsensical, and the Malkavian being extra personal as I'm a mental patient myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T09:19:43-07:00","id":1464202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464173#post1464173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prior to v5 most of them dressed proffesional with a few occult references. I can't recall how they dress now but I recall the costume sketches in core were pretty distinctive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I especially like this Tremere picture from the first Clanbook, <a href=\"https://ibb.co/MsT1NGJ\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/MsT1NGJ </a>. Simple, unassuming, straightforward, and makes a good impression.<br /> There is no indication in the book, but I think this is actually Inner Counsellor Thomas Wyncham. Very similar to <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/f/f9/TW.png/revision/latest?cb=20160104175543\" target=\"_blank\">https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/wh...20160104175543</a> , including the electricity-like effect (possibly it is from Path of the Levinbolt).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464174#post1464174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate the costume sketches in V5 core, for every single clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The single pictures that usually accompany Clan descriptions seem more evocative to me than the multitude that V5 gives. And in general, the pre-V5 art seems much more characterful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2021, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T12:25:56-07:00","id":1464213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464173#post1464173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prior to v5 most of them dressed proffesional with a few occult references. I can't recall how they dress now but I recall the costume sketches in core were pretty distinctive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you dress for your profession and Elif's is &quot;sexy bartender.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href