com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:15:57-07:00","id":1464345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464271#post1464271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of which is appropriate for a bartender running a nightclub.<br /> <br /> Or is your objection that a Tremere is running a Succubus club style establishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Becoming a vampire of clan tremere and then spending eternity as bar staff is a depressing thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:50:29-07:00","id":1464350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464345#post1464345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Becoming a vampire of clan tremere and then spending eternity as bar staff is a depressing thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a nine-to-five barbarian!<br /> Don't have to do no paperwork, I'm happy as a clam<br /> Not a farmer or librarian!<br /> I'm a killer with a vengeance and a profit-sharing plan<br /> <br /> Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, and Toreador have it easy. They have the toolkit for easy living baked into their disciplines. Gangrel though? Nosferatu? Malkavians? You try turning &quot;heightens emotions&quot; into a rent-paying skillset. Or worse, you could be stuck with Protean 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:49:31-07:00","id":1464367,"title":"","content":"A Hot Tremere... Sure. Intelligence does correlate with looks. <br /> A Tremere who spends her time as a bartender.... Erhm.... Why do you have Dominate again? Is the Chantry cool with this? Is this some insidious Tremere ploy? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, and Toreador have it easy. They have the toolkit for easy living baked into their disciplines. Gangrel though? Nosferatu? Malkavians? You try turning &quot;heightens emotions&quot; into a rent-paying skillset. Or worse, you could be stuck with Protean 3. </div> </div> </div>Eh. Gangrel are the only big clan that really don't have an &quot;easy living&quot; discipline (until animalism 3, that's a hunter's dream). Nosferatu are arguably the strongest clan discipline wise in terms of unliving. I think you're underselling obfuscate massively. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:01:43-07:00","id":1464373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464367#post1464367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hot Tremere... Sure. Intelligence does correlate with looks.<br /> A Tremere who spends her time as a bartender.... Erhm.... Why do you have Dominate again? Is the Chantry cool with this? Is this some insidious Tremere ploy?<br /> <br /> <br /> Eh. Gangrel are the only big clan that really don't have an &quot;easy living&quot; discipline (until animalism 3, that's a hunter's dream). Nosferatu are arguably the strongest clan discipline wise in terms of unliving. I think you're underselling obfuscate massively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate will get you easy basic living (through shoplifting), but getting stable income will require breaking into industrial espionage or something, which takes additional skillsets beyond &quot;is invisible (except to cameras)&quot;. You can do it, but it's a lot more effort than &quot;Has Dominate 2&quot; and &quot;Has Presence 1&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:18:01-07:00","id":1464376,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking vampires tend to have the skills to go with their disciplines. Dominate is a really strong discipline, but next to useless without Manipulation, intimidation, leadership, subterfuge. Obfuscate needs Manipulation, stealth and subterfuge, with performance if you want to lean in on Mask. Mask of a thousand faces is a god-skill if you get creative with it. Take five minutes and just think of all the things you could do!<br /> <br /> Disciplines also aren't in a vacuum. You've still got your other vampire abilities. Using obfuscate to sneak in some blood bonds? Great. That's you sorted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:26:04-07:00","id":1464377,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Elif even has a job besides her Tremere work? In the trailer, she's standing on the terrace of a club. In one of trailers, she's hunting on the dance floor. Given that one of the Seattle Tremere is biggest selling points to hirelings is how good their hunting grounds are, Elif might have a personal responsibility to keep at least one bar busy and amenable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T09:50:37-07:00","id":1464387,"title":"","content":"Given that Elif is working with you to steal information from Slug, I think people forget that running a nightclub puts her at the center of Kindred social life and intelligence.<br /> <br /> But are we actually complaining she's LESS stereotypical as a vampire of her Clan?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T10:28:53-07:00","id":1464390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464377#post1464377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if Elif even has a job besides her Tremere work? In the trailer, she's standing on the terrace of a club. In one of trailers, she's hunting on the dance floor. Given that one of the Seattle Tremere is biggest selling points to hirelings is how good their hunting grounds are, Elif might have a personal responsibility to keep at least one bar busy and amenable.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464367#post1464367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Tremere who spends her time as a bartender.... Erhm.... Why do you have Dominate again? Is the Chantry cool with this? Is this some insidious Tremere ploy?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think she is not part of the club's staff. If it is somehow her club, then possibly she is the owner, but more likely she has the management blood bonded or ghouled, or is working on it. <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/the-newcomers\" target=\"_blank\">It is written</a> that Elif is the right hand of the Victor Goga, the Tremere leader of the Newcomers faction, so her hanging around at the nightclub is likely part of the faction's movements in Seattle.<br /> <br /> As I see it Kindred never hold regular 8-hour jobs, unless it is some very specific plot or everything is arranged for their convenience at the job. And in the latter case, it is not actually an 8-hour job anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464350#post1464350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue, Brujah, Tremere, and Toreador have it easy. They have the toolkit for easy living baked into their disciplines. Gangrel though? Nosferatu? Malkavians? You try turning &quot;heightens emotions&quot; into a rent-paying skillset. Or worse, you could be stuck with Protean 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is always blood bonding and ghouling for a Vampire to fall back on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464367#post1464367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hot Tremere... Sure. Intelligence does correlate with looks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aisling is quite hot as well, <a href=\"https://ibb.co/gD12sb6\" target=\"_blank\">in a nerdy sort of way.</a> The character art from the VtM New York graphic novel games is so evocative and nicely done. Carna is another beautiful Tremere, <a href=\"https://ibb.co/GxcKcrk\" target=\"_blank\">of course</a>. And then there is <a href=\"https://ibb.co/CbZ9jnD\" target=\"_blank\">this nice picture </a>from the first Tremere Clanbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-18-2021, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T11:48:37-07:00","id":1464397,"title":"","content":"I mean, maybe she is a failure as a wizard (or doesn't consider her bag) and decided to run a club instead. Its not like she's going to be killed for not getting straight A's in potions and obscuromancy.<br /> <br /> Let's face it, way too many Clans are just Thing A and never thing B.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T23:53:37-07:00","id":1464469,"title":"","content":"My issue is that for many people, this'll be their intro to the series, so going against stereotypes for the main representative of a clan is really going to give people a misleading idea about the setting. Bloodlines 1 mostly gave us great examples of the different clans. Brujah and Toreador need not be mentioned (though i would've appreciated Camarilla Brujah), the Nosferatu are perfectly displayed in all their glory, Voremans are great malkavians (I really like the voice overs for the professor, but the mansion is too much) Strauss is great. LaCroix is a pathetic example of a Ventrue and the only example in game beyond a few voiceless mooks, but he does get a lot of ideas about the ventrue across (even if they're mostly reduced to the negative facets) <br /> <br /> While the Tremere can use &quot;faces&quot; I'd think they'd pick less controversial choices. Remember this is a clan that exercises a lot of control over it's members and it's members in turn control themselves for the good of the organization that shelters them. <br /> Unless you meet a bunch of stereotypical tremere to balance it out, it's not a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T05:35:06-07:00","id":1464509,"title":"","content":"If you look at the example outfits in Core V5, she fits right in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T08:41:16-07:00","id":1464516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464469#post1464469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is that for many people, this'll be their intro to the series, so going against stereotypes for the main representative of a clan is really going to give people a misleading idea about the setting. Bloodlines 1 mostly gave us great examples of the different clans. Brujah and Toreador need not be mentioned (though i would've appreciated Camarilla Brujah), the Nosferatu are perfectly displayed in all their glory, Voremans are great malkavians (I really like the voice overs for the professor, but the mansion is too much) Strauss is great. LaCroix is a pathetic example of a Ventrue and the only example in game beyond a few voiceless mooks, but he does get a lot of ideas about the ventrue across (even if they're mostly reduced to the negative facets)<br /> <br /> While the Tremere can use &quot;faces&quot; I'd think they'd pick less controversial choices. Remember this is a clan that exercises a lot of control over it's members and it's members in turn control themselves for the good of the organization that shelters them.<br /> Unless you meet a bunch of stereotypical tremere to balance it out, it's not a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that she has a necklace with a pyramid that indicates she is a Tremere. It subtly shows how the Pyramid's influence reaches In all sorts of places.<br /> We already have Strauss in <i>Bloodlines 1</i> meeting the PC in a Chantry, and Aisling and her Childe Agathon staying on top of a mundane esoteric shop in <i>Coteries of New York</i>. So I think it fits that we get a differently placed Tremere in the next VtM video game. And because Elif is at the forefront of the game, there <a href=\"https://kolekcjonerki.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-edycja-kolekcjonerska.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">will also be a miniature</a> of a Tremere Vampire produced <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Assuming the game will be released...Hopefully, it will be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464397#post1464397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's face it, way too many Clans are just Thing A and never thing B.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually an example of a Tremere Neonate in the Revised Clanbook. who is a nightclub owner. Also, the example Coterie has Varya Korlov, who is noted as very often using her appearance in attempts to influence mortals and other Kindred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464509#post1464509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the example outfits in Core V5, she fits right in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about this, these outfits do look at least slightly occult, while Elif is simply dressed as if she was having a nights out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-19-2021, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T11:17:24-07:00","id":1464524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464509#post1464509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the example outfits in Core V5, she fits right in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that, she looks pretty cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T01:28:52-07:00","id":1464569,"title":"","content":"I actually think Strauss is actually a little too suave for Tremere. His mannerisms are very nice. He's a captivating speaker with a buttery voice. You'd think he had Presence as an in-clan discipline. . His outfit is silly, but everything is very silly in bloodlines 1. When everyone walks like they're on a catwalk, a red trenchcoat doesn't really stand out so much. B2 seems a lot more down to earth artistically, so the folk who stand out really stand out. <br /> <br /> IDK what the party scene is like in seatle. But I'm really curious as to how Tremere are in on the party scene. It's also unusual to see physically attractive people embrace counterculture, nevermind tremere who are all about conformity. Perhaps if she was someone who always wore a different outfit, it'd be interesting, but game design tends to favour putting folk in the same outfits all the time to stand out. <br /> <br /> And yes, I realize I'm being far too anal trying to articulate what the issues are, but there are plentiful people that just know they don't like something and don't try to explain why. I don't hate it, it's not the nuCam, I just don't like it to an extent that I think it's worth pointing out. Most of the characters shown in B2 have made me a little iffy, and not because they're sick bastards that make artworks out of a captured family (but because someone who does make such artworks is going to be destroyed and it's a dumb idea.) <br /> <br /> <br /> I think an inherently challenging thing about adapting VTM to other media is that, well, you need characters to visually stand out, when really they want to fit in and be unseen. But then you also confound this issue with the WoD being a GTA-like Joke setting where fast food turns you into a monster and the fossil fuel companies are trying to dig up demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T02:53:15-07:00","id":1464574,"title":"","content":"You leave Strauss and his buttery smooth voice alone! Hands down my favorite NPC from <i>Bloodlines,</i> and that's 90% due to Jim Ward's vocal performance. Strauss is just the right amount of suave for a powerful Tremere. The only problem is that any Ventrue worth their salt should be even <i>more</i> suave and likeable, which just highlights what a complete clown show LaCroix is.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, isn't LaCroix the only major Ventrue NPC in the game? What a travesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T08:44:33-07:00","id":1464591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464569#post1464569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think Strauss is actually a little too suave for Tremere. His mannerisms are very nice. He's a captivating speaker with a buttery voice. You'd think he had Presence as an in-clan discipline. . His outfit is silly, but everything is very silly in bloodlines 1. When everyone walks like they're on a catwalk, a red trenchcoat doesn't really stand out so much. B2 seems a lot more down to earth artistically, so the folk who stand out really stand out.<br /> <br /> IDK what the party scene is like in seatle. But I'm really curious as to how Tremere are in on the party scene. It's also unusual to see physically attractive people embrace counterculture, nevermind tremere who are all about conformity. Perhaps if she was someone who always wore a different outfit, it'd be interesting, but game design tends to favour putting folk in the same outfits all the time to stand out.<br /> <br /> And yes, I realize I'm being far too anal trying to articulate what the issues are, but there are plentiful people that just know they don't like something and don't try to explain why. I don't hate it, it's not the nuCam, I just don't like it to an extent that I think it's worth pointing out. Most of the characters shown in B2 have made me a little iffy, and not because they're sick bastards that make artworks out of a captured family (but because someone who does make such artworks is going to be destroyed and it's a dumb idea.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I think an inherently challenging thing about adapting VTM to other media is that, well, you need characters to visually stand out, when really they want to fit in and be unseen. But then you also confound this issue with the WoD being a GTA-like Joke setting where fast food turns you into a monster and the fossil fuel companies are trying to dig up demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's just silly. EVERY Tremere has a Manipulation of at least 4 and most have it as about 5. Of course they're going to have deep smooth voices that convince you to accept their Devil's bargains.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But it should be noted that vampires and the party scene are inherently linked because of the blood supply and information to be gained by them too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-20-2021, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T09:45:15-07:00","id":1464594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464591#post1464591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it should be noted that vampires and the party scene are inherently linked because of the blood supply and information to be gained by them too.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the money aspect,, but I just checked on google and it does not appear to be that much. Though a Vampire can bolster the income through running various illicit activities at the club. Also, a nightclub is a nice location for Kindred to meet up for business and mingling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464574#post1464574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, isn't LaCroix the only major Ventrue NPC in the game? What a travesty.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember he is the only one. I think there are also some Ventrue Kindred as enemies in the final level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464569#post1464569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> His outfit is silly, but everything is very silly in bloodlines 1. When everyone walks like they're on a catwalk, a red trenchcoat doesn't really stand out so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he saw how Jeanette and VV dress and decided he needs to fit in ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though I think he doesn't look that silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464569#post1464569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) I just don't like it to an extent that I think it's worth pointing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows, a <i>Bloodlines 2</i> writer or developer might just be reading this thread, and maybe they will take what you wrote into account.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464569#post1464569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an inherently challenging thing about adapting VTM to other media is that, well, you need characters to visually stand out, when really they want to fit in and be unseen. But then you also confound this issue with the WoD being a GTA-like Joke setting where fast food turns you into a monster and the fossil fuel companies are trying to dig up demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate in regard to WoD being a joke setting?<br /> <br /> By the way, did you know that in <i>Bloodlines 1</i> if you dance in a club for around five minutes, you regain a point of Humanity? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Can be done once per club. The power and joy of clubbing on a nights out...if only it would be this easy for the Kindred in VtM...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-20-2021, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:31:52-07:00","id":1464616,"title":"","content":"Pentex. Like all of it. Every damn product. Read any book of the wyrm. There are plenty of parody companies. <br /> Their technocratic equivolents. <br /> There's a potentially funny level of satire to the whole Jyhad and vampires essentially being caricacatures of the elite. <br /> Bloodlines 1 also had a lot of joke brands. The Energy drink vending machines sell &quot;demon seed&quot; for example. You also had some very humourous radio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:55:07-07:00","id":1464624,"title":"","content":"I think the funniest thing about Pentex is they went to exaggerated cartoonish levels about what they did and their pollution only to find out in 2016 through 2020 that most of them were not far enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T17:37:34-07:00","id":1464665,"title":"","content":"I just can't wrap my head around any of the complaints about Elif here. I'll state them as I'm reading them, not saying that this is necessarily what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> meant.<br /> <br /> An intelligent woman can't be beautiful. A beautiful woman can't embrace counterculture. Someone must embrace counterculture to dress like the part. You can't be an academic type and like clubs. You can't exist within a structured society without agreeing with it. Beautiful women are conservatives. Vampires universally want to be discreet in their wardrobe. Video Games have an obligation to present the correct stereotypes to new players. New players will have their impression of a clan marked forever by the game's characters. Tremere don't like being beautiful or dressing for parties even when they go to one.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that one of the few things BL' did wrong was to rely so heavily on stereotypes. It should have none whatsoever except by coincidence, nothing at all should indicate a character's clan just by appearance or behavior, except for the Nos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T17:43:54-07:00","id":1464666,"title":"","content":"I think MWIS has a very specific idea of how Tremere act and dress.<br /> <br /> Very specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:42:41-07:00","id":1464697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464624#post1464624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the funniest thing about Pentex is they went to exaggerated cartoonish levels about what they did and their pollution only to find out in 2016 through 2020 that most of them were not far enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>We didn't need to wait until 2016 for that; the writing was on the wall with Subsidiaries (I think the writers did some digging into shady corporate shit for that, inspired by the fall of the real world Enron), and Deepwater Horizon was in 2010. The scientific community has also been unanimous in grave concerns about global climate change from anthropogenic CO2 for decades now. It's a real kick in the pants that including any of that in the 90s would have resulting in a call to cut back your crude agenda, when even the W:tA books were talking about how Endron manages to make itself look like a green, positive company through PR, and labels anyone who takes further action as a tree-hugging hippy... back about the mid-90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T01:13:36-07:00","id":1464706,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying it can't happen. <br /> I just think these three things have negative correlations with one another<br /> <br /> Tremere<br /> Attractive<br /> Embraces counterculture<br /> <br /> So my &quot;this is a self insert&quot; flags have gone right up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:04:17-07:00","id":1464763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464706#post1464706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying it can't happen.<br /> I just think these three things have negative correlations with one another<br /> <br /> Tremere<br /> Attractive<br /> Embraces counterculture<br /> <br /> So my &quot;this is a self insert&quot; flags have gone right up.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you say that Elif is into counterculture just from the way she dresses? Maybe she just likes the look, or maybe she does for the sake of establishing herself at this nightclub. Antoinette Sauveterre (A Bahari Toreador Seraphim of the Tal'Mahe'Ra) is said to dress in street casual and business casual - would you suggest that this means she has a relaxed and easygoing attitude? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Her description says otherwise.<br /> <br /> It would be nice if in <i>VtM:</i> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> some NPCs would change their appearance based on the location and point in the storyline. So later we might see Elif in casual but less revealing clothing, or in a classic robe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2021, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:29:25-07:00","id":1464771,"title":"","content":"Isn't the self insert criticism not normally used when a character looks ugly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T20:20:10-07:00","id":1464819,"title":"","content":"Tremere gotta eat too and nightclubs are a good place to pick up your next meal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T20:30:22-07:00","id":1464820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464819#post1464819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere gotta eat too and nightclubs are a good place to pick up your next meal...</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I liked was apparently everyone in Seattle wanted to be part of the Blood Trade.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:27:50-07:00","id":1464847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464706#post1464706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying it can't happen.<br /> I just think these three things have negative correlations with one another<br /> <br /> Tremere<br /> Attractive<br /> Embraces counterculture<br /> <br /> So my &quot;this is a self insert&quot; flags have gone right up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally disagree, but the forum ate my arguments twice already and I'm on my phone, so whatever.<br /> <br /> What's the problem with self inserts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T05:28:12-07:00","id":1464861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464847#post1464847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally disagree, but the forum ate my arguments twice already and I'm on my phone, so whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh how I've felt your pain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the problem with self inserts? </div> </div> </div>It correlates with a lot of other issues. It doesn't necessarily garantee it, but the pattern is there. <br /> <br /> 1: People who like idealized self inserts are often protective over their characters and don't like them to fail or get challenged on a moral or authoritative level. If it's just another player, the harm is limited. If it's the game master, oh boy. In pen and paper you can try and go against or poke holes in the stupid plan your GM wholeheartedly believes is really clever, but then your character might risk drawing onto yourself the hostile contrivances of fate or you'll have an OoC issue. In a computer game, the option won't even be there. You'll have fallout 4 level dialogue options of &quot;Yes&quot; &quot;Yes MAM&quot; &quot;Yes but Sarcastic&quot; and &quot;Let me postpone my unavoidable agreement&quot;. <br /> <br /> Dominate did B1 such a massive favour. &quot;You will get the ship's manifest&quot; &quot;Fuck you&quot; <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>&quot;You will get the ship's manifest&quot;</i> &quot;</span></span></span> I<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> will get the ship's manifest&quot;. But when you're just going along with things because X character is the writer but perfect and of course you're going to agree with her... I don't like that. <br /> <br /> <br /> My other problem with self inserts is context. I realize it might be hard for some to act out a different person or to understand the values of a very different culture, but the setting suffers when it has to be viewed through a the lense of a sheltered middle class liberal. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T06:45:24-07:00","id":1464865,"title":"","content":"I personally think WoD is a bad place for self-inserts as well, Simply put your pc is very fragile and will die with ease.Especially Vampire because Vampires are assholes.<br /> <br /> Just play d&amp;d if you want to roll with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T08:59:20-07:00","id":1464877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464861#post1464861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh how I've felt your pain.<br /> Dominate did B1 such a massive favour. &quot;You will get the ship's manifest&quot; &quot;Fuck you&quot; <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>&quot;You will get the ship's manifest&quot;</i> &quot;</span></span></span> I[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px] will get the ship's manifest&quot;. But when you're just going along with things because X character is the writer but perfect and of course you're going to agree with her... I don't like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is this cool detail with how LaCroix attempts to use Dominate on the <i>Bloodlines 1</i> protagonist at the end, but it does not work. A little mystery - did LaCroix just fumble with it, or did somebody else intervene, or is the PC actually of lower Generation than LaCroix? (The potency of the Vitae needs time to do its work, hence the PC is vulnerable to Dominate at the start of the game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T09:48:32-07:00","id":1464881,"title":"","content":"The fact that some people use this forum mostly on phone is a statement to the quality of our community. Because the engine just sucks.<br /> <br /> My take on self inserts is that they make problems easier to spot more than cause them. A self insert isn't a bad thing, but a bad writer makes bad self inserts.<br /> <br /> So putting aside that I didn't saw as many red flags as you, nor see her as embracing counter culture just for the way she dresses, I'm not worried if she is a self insert. I am worried by the history of this game's development, though.<br /> <br /> And self inserts aren't better off in D&amp;D, that's a silly statement. Those characters are far more squishy in early levels and starting off stronger is just as possible on both. A bad self insert will also be equally problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:38:39-07:00","id":1464922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1464865#post1464865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think WoD is a bad place for self-inserts as well, Simply put your pc is very fragile and will die with ease.Especially Vampire because Vampires are assholes.<br /> <br /> Just play d&amp;d if you want to roll with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of another dragon game derailment, some editions also sport very, very fragile characters that wouldn't want to get into combat. The earliest ones, in fact, though 5th doesn't exactly stray far from there. They just get a guarantee of around 6 starting hp instead of possibly rolling a 1... and having only one spell per day and a dagger. Such is the thing of adventurer-killing housecat memes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T17:04:19-07:00","id":1464939,"title":"","content":"Not to be coy, MWIS, but I imagine Elif is there because they need a iconic &quot;face&quot; for the product. She's the female face and Mr. Damp is the male.<br /> <br /> Both designed for sex appeal. though Elif is more so because, well, sexism in Hollywood.<br /> <br /> Mind you, vampire games should be sensual but the first game didn't provide much for the straight female/gay male audience.<br /> <br /> (Albeit Nines and La Croix both remain very popular)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-22-2021, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T08:03:57-07:00","id":1465011,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\">I have watched the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_oYJAnhvgNk\" target=\"_blank\">gameplay demo</a> from E3 2019 again. Some observations:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">-The conversations with Elif and the Nosferatu NPC should be at least two to three times longer, with some dialogue options asking for additional information, personal details, or recent rumors.<br /> I have to say one of my favorite games is <i>Planescape: Torment</i>, which has so much text that it is like reading a book...I'm not saying that I expect other RPGs to be like this, but certainly more content in the dialogues is possible and would make <i>Bloodlines 2</i> a much better game.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">-The Thinblood Disciplines are a cool idea, a nice callback to Thinblood Inceptors and a showing of the potential of Vampires. Though I have to say that I am aversive to the idea of Nebulation, because it disrupts my idea of supernatural capabilities in WoD. Turning into mist requires Protean 5, after all...which implies it is a high-end feat.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Chiropteran and Mentalism are fine. Chiropteran seems very characterful, calling upon the idea of bats being somehow mystically related to Vampires.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">(Fun fact: Even Kindred who have never seen a bat or a wolf assume these forms when using Protean 4. This was tested with a person specifically brought up in a controlled environment before being embraced and taught Protean 4.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">-There is too much combat for a starting quest. I very much like how in <i>Bloodlines 1</i> Santa Monica has very little combat, and it is all about dialogues, running errands, exploration, and investigation. If the developers want the quest to be challenging, then the enemies could be reduced in numbers, but made individually stronger.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">-The area the PC has to traverse in the quest seems to be just right for a starting task. Helps the player get into the mood and atmosphere of the game.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-23-2021, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T12:28:24-07:00","id":1465025,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that first quests in <i>Bloodlines</i> have little combat as you can choose to go on combat mode or not in many places, but in general Santa Monica was very well designed as a playground to learn your style of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T12:32:34-07:00","id":1465026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1465025#post1465025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say that first quests in <i>Bloodlines</i> have little combat as you can choose to go on combat mode or not in many places, but in general Santa Monica was very well designed as a playground to learn your style of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is they chose the murder-y route for reaching Slug but there's multiple ways of reaching him. I figure you can probably pass the people through stealth or conversation.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if it plays more like Deus Ex: Human Revolution than Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T02:23:05-07:00","id":1465111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463949-news-bloodlines-2-is-not-cancelled-but-almost-was?p=1465026#post1465026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't be surprised if it plays more like Deus Ex: Human Revolution than Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>HR would be pretty good (even if it's a shadow of the original game in most ways) <br /> <br /> I think HR takes it too far, but I think the game would benefit a lot from rewarding not-killing in most conflicts. (but occasionally the game should be punishing you for not killing when the context demands it; people should play smart and think for themselves, not just follow whatever gives you a score of xp) <br /> <br /> To me, a linear vampire game isn't just about completing objectives, vampire is about completing objectives and not making a massive mess of things, or trying to patch up the massive mess you made of things, or trying to patch up the patch-up of the massive mess you made of things. Alas, it'd be very hard to transfer that sense of responsibility to a game where every option needs to be coded and thus there can't be that many options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}